from a beef between show hosts to a beef  between co-hosts Ridiculousness may have  been known for its Wild video clips but  it was nothing compared to what happened  behind the scenes  at the beginning of every episode a  warning tells viewers not to attempt any  stunts or activities presented  throughout the show it also condemns the  submission of videos of any kind from  viewers if Ridiculousness doesn't accept  submissions then where are they getting  their Clips since the viral videos come  from the internet it sounds as simple as  a Google search but licensing is a  tricky business in a 2019 interview with  John interviews host Rob Dyrdek revealed  he isn't the one searching for the  videos but instead has a massive  organization that handles the process a  team of people scours the internet and  when the perfect video is found they try  to make contact with the video's  original uploader distractify notes that  someone on Reddit claimed to receive a  one-time 200 payment for their video  it's unclear if this is a regular  practice for the show but with an  endless supply of videos online we don't  have to worry about Rob running out of  hilarious content  talk about a major ear worm if you're  not old enough to know of the hit 80s  rock band Devo you might think the  catchy theme song came from  Ridiculousness however the theme song is  actually a cover of Devo's  uncontrollable urge from the band's  classic debut album Q are we not men a  we Are Devo in season 4 episode 9 of  Fantasy Factory Deer dick teams up with  Devo band member Mark mothersbaugh to  record the cover for Ridiculousness  mother's ball has an expansive career  himself along with co-founding the band  Devo his solo Endeavors have included  composing music for film and TV such as  Nickelodeon's Rugrats and Wes Anderson's  features bottle rocket Rushmore the  Royal Tenenbaums and The Life Aquatic  with Steve zisu so next time the  Ridiculousness theme song gets stuck in  your head you know who to blame  Ridiculousness isn't only big in the U.S  the show airs all around the globe but  instead of dubbing episodes each country  gets its own hosts reacting to Clips in  2015 ridiculous Chile was the first  international version of the show  followed by ridiculous made in France  verguenza Hena made in Spain and more in  2016. the effective format of  ridiculousness has also been used in  multiple spin-offs including MTV's  amazingness deliciousness messiness and  adorableness the first spin-off  amazingness deviated the most from the  Ridiculousness format hosted by Dyrdek  himself the talent competition ran from  December 2017 to January 2018 featuring  six contestants performing in front of  judges Chris Drama faff Eddie Huang and  Crystal b a ten thousand dollar prize  was awarded to the final performer  standing the other three spin-offs do  not feature deer deck but they stay true  to his style Tiffany Thiessen  commentates on disastrous food related  Clips on deliciousness James Davis  commentates on the kind of clips that  make you cry out awe on adorableness and  Snooki commentates on pure Chaos on  messiness  MTV's launch in 1981 changed the course  of Television by being the first to air  24 7 music related programming and music  videos however with the internet  offering a new way for fans to access  music content the network pivoted to the  reality programming genre this jarring  change in content devastated an entire  generation but on August 1st 2021 MTV's  40th anniversary the network had the  perfect opportunity to cater to longtime  viewers when scheduling was announced  Gen X was disappointed all over again  instead of the usual 113 hours a week of  ridiculousness MTV celebrated its  birthday by playing the show for 24  hours straight Twitter users and Outlets  such as bar stool Sports expressed their  outrage while Ridiculousness fans  celebrated in the background  a hot topic of discussion around  Ridiculousness is the longtime feud  between dear deck and Daniel Tosh of  Tosh.0 it all started with a tweet from  Tosh congrats Rob Dyrdek new show looks  very funny and familiar dear deck  tweeted back thank you so much Daniel  Tosh maybe later this week you Bob Saget  and Tom Bergeron can come down to my  factory and play in an interview with  Larry King deer deck revealed that both  Ridiculousness and Fantasy Factory were  pitched and sold before Tosh.0 aired but  Fantasy Factory was produced first  by the time my Ridiculousness came out  it was already after the first season of  Tosh came out right it can be argued  there are more differences between the  shows than similarities the comedy  styles are on opposite sides of the  spectrum with Tosh.0 taking a more  scripted approach and sprinkling skits  into episodes the argument between the  two came to a head when Tosh featured a  sketch targeting deer deck for copying  his Show's premise in a now deleted  tweet deerdeck responded with I am not a  comedian or an actor so unfortunately  for Daniel Tosh we are going to have to  settle this the old-fashioned way this  was followed by Tasha's tweet fair  enough but if you have to beat me up can  we film it and put it on my show so  people will actually watch it  deirdex co-hosts Chanel West Coast and  Stilo brim play a significant role in  the show's success brim controls the  playback of the clips slowing down  rewinding and zooming in on the funniest  moments and it isn't an episode of  Ridiculousness without Chanel's  contagious laugh so how did deer deck  find his two co-hosts Chicago native  Steelo Brim moved to Los Angeles to  pursue a music career brim told CBS news  that he was helping deirdek's cousin  start a publishing and production  company when he met Rob Rob you still  having to come to the studio like twice  and she's like hey man you're funny you  should do a show together  deer deck followed through by bringing  on brim as co-host of ridiculousness he  also regularly appeared in Fantasy  Factory and dear deck's animation series  Wild Grinders as the voice of meaty in  an interview on the podcast no jumper  Chanel explained how she managed to meet  deer deck through Myspace I would go and  I would add all the top artists on  MySpace and then I'd add all their top  friends one of those artists was dear  deck's cousin Chris dramafaff through a  friendship with him Chanel met dear deck  and hit it off the rest as they say is  history  yet another Feud Sparks between Chanel  West Coast and radio hosts Charlemagne  the God in episode 26 of season 9  Charlemagne appears as a guest host on  the show during the episode Charlemagne  says he values being straightforward  with people and not being afraid to  convey his opinions to people's faces  one of those opinions is about Chanel's  rapping abilities  I told her she was whack rapping one  time Chanel defended herself against the  claims  saying though you can have opinions it  doesn't mean they're right though she  then flaunts her long list of  accomplishments as an established artist  Outlets blew the story up but Chanel  admits the beef didn't last more than  five minutes she tells too Fab it's not  so much that I took it personally it's  that I knew he was stating I was a whack  rapper on a platform where all my fans  were watching the last thing I was gonna  do was let somebody call me a whack  rapper and not use that time right there  to State the facts and set things  straight  can you think of a better job than  getting to react to funny videos all day  long with your friends still that  doesn't take away from how much hard  work it takes to film hundreds of  episodes over the course of 28 Seasons  what started as filming a single episode  for 12 hours turned into filming six  episodes daily brim attributes this  change to the hosts taking on a more  improvisational style each episode calls  for an outfit change and the host's  energy varies depending on how early or  late the production is into filming  Chanel told in touch that there's a  reason why she sometimes looks tired if  you ever see me looking a little extra  tired it's probably either the last  episode of the day or it's the first  episode of the day where I was still  really tired  deer deck never wanted to be the old guy  on TV his one true passion has always  been entrepreneurship but it was  impossible to pass up the money that  came with his shows on MTV in an  interview with graham bensinger Dyrdek  talked about how he almost walked away  from Ridiculousness I don't want to be  on MTV when I'm when I'm 40. I don't  want to be Kurt loader it's no secret  that money has played a significant role  in Deer deck's longtime partnership with  MTV so how much does he make from  Ridiculousness in an interview on Jason  tartik's podcast trading Secrets deer  deck revealed the number they would only  pay me thirty five thousand dollars an  episode to do Ridiculousness and then  they offered me the 125 000 and then  when I got the integration rights then  I'm like I'm just gonna do this because  I can just make millions doing this  later on three shows in with MTV Dyrdek  said I was able to get way more money  based on the success of what had  happened with Fantasy Factory of course  that 125 thousand dollars is just the  talent fee that number doesn't even  include the money made from integration  deals that deerduck took advantage of in  all his shows deirdek explained that if  MTV didn't offer a massive paycheck  season 4 would have ended his hosting  gig for Ridiculousness MTV knew the  stakes were high so when it came to  negotiations deirdek had a leg up and  got an offer he couldn't refuse after  the signing of the contract deirdek  called MTV a great partner as an  entrepreneur Dyrdek didn't just get  lucky he knew exactly what he was doing  and used his platform on MTV as a way to  make millions elsewhere the entire  premise of fantasy factory was tailored  around product integration deer deck  would write intricate integrated brand  Partnerships with advertisers into the  show and then would use those same  advertisers to make other big deals on  the side for his own Ventures whether  he's promoting clothing brands by  wearing them on Robin big and  Ridiculousness or doing stunts in a  Carl's Jr costume on Fantasy Factory  Deer deck's Savvy marketing skills  granted him ability to broaden his  financial reach beyond the MTV Network  in addition to a fun laugh filled Time  Each episode of Ridiculousness offers a  variety of star-studded guest hosts some  of the most popular appearances include  from riffraff and Ray J from season 3  Kendall and Kylie Jenner from season 5  Eric Andre from season 6 8 and 20 and  dear deck's frequent collaborator  Christopher Big Black Boykin who  tragically passed in 2017. more recent  episodes have seen a decline in  Celebrity guest hosts but some of the  show's most memorable moments can be  linked to their many guests take for  example an episode with Kevin Hart where  an entire segment titled big ass man  pigeons was inspired by Hart's fearful  encounter with an ostrich he didn't move  his body but his head like spent all the  way around and he started following me  and I was like yo man get the [ __ ] out  of here  only Ridiculousness can think of a  connection like that or Eric Andre's  visits which largely consists of him  flirting with co-host Chanel West Coast  and an email's worth of swear words that  needed to be censored after taping one  way or another celebrities are always  bringing something special to  ridiculousness  most people aren't familiar with Chanel  West Coast's long-term connection to the  Ridiculousness Studio Chanel has taken  many different Avenues in her career  from recording music to acting in MTV's  the hard times of RJ Berger to becoming  a supporting cast member on the reality  TV series Love and Hip Hop Hollywood  however as Chanel told in touch a  recurring theme in her career has always  been the Hollywood center Studio where  Ridiculousness does its filming and  there's some there's like this weird  Divine thing about this studio like my  first job was there and then I ended up  filming Ridiculousness there maybe we  can attribute the great success of  ridiculousness to this magical  occurrence one can only hope Chanel's  future endeavors will have her revisit  the studio time and time again  thank you
 

